{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774862521,"nonce":"OAdxqdJxDLrv4T4H54DAshLmhLk=","title":"Review container launch is fire-and-forget with no error recovery","message":"When a coder session completes and transitions to reviewing, the review container launch can silently fail, leaving the coder session permanently stuck in \"reviewing\" status with no recovery path.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThree compounding issues:\n\n### 1. _launch_background discards Popen handle\n`host/watcher/host_watcher.py:_launch_background()` fires subprocess.Popen but discards the handle. Nobody ever checks the exit code. If launch.py fails (Docker issue, git worktree issue, tracker issue, stale container name), the error goes only to watcher.log file (not the main watcher logger) and is silently lost. Also leaks the file handle on every call (never closes the opened log file).\n\n### 2. Status set to \"reviewing\" before launch, never reverted\n`host/watcher/review_orchestrator.py:maybe_launch_review()` sets coder status to \"reviewing\" BEFORE calling _launch_background. If the background process fails, no code path reverts the status. The session is permanently stuck.\n\n### 3. Orphan detector ignores \"reviewing\" status\n`host/watcher/session_monitor.py:maybe_resume_orphan()` only handles \"working\", \"starting\", and \"waiting:review\" statuses. A coder session stuck in \"reviewing\" is a dead end — never auto-resumed, never picked up for review again, never cleaned up.\n\n## Failure Scenario\n\n1. Coder session reaches waiting:review\n2. maybe_launch_review sets coder status to \"reviewing\" and fires _launch_background\n3. launch.py runs in background and fails (any of many reasons)\n4. Error goes to watcher.log file, not the main watcher log\n5. Nobody checks the exit code\n6. Coder session permanently stuck in \"reviewing\"\n7. Orphan detector ignores it\n8. check_for_auto_review skips it (not waiting:review)\n9. Session is permanently dead\n\n## Fix Required\n\n1. **Track Popen handles in _launch_background.** Store the Popen object. Add a periodic check (in the watcher main loop or session_monitor) that polls recently launched subprocesses for early exits. On non-zero exit: log the error prominently and revert the coder session status to waiting:review so it can be retried.\n\n2. **Fix the file handle leak.** Close the file handle after Popen (the subprocess inherits the fd).\n\n3. **Add \"reviewing\" recovery to orphan detector.** If a coder session is in \"reviewing\" status, the corresponding review container doesn't exist (docker ps), and it's not in _recently_launched (or the grace period expired), revert the coder session to waiting:review.\n\n## Frequency\n\n~50% of review cycles in observed sessions (6+ failures across ~20 reviews).\n\nREQ: REQ-009 (review lifecycle)","files":null}]}